"Sammiel" <lowrysam@gmail.com> writes:
> I just found out that bows are not two-handed weapons, which means you
> can #twoweapon with them! This is particularly awesome for Samurai, who
> can wield their katana in one hand, and have the bow ready for instant
> firing in the other.

Missiles will only be fired (as opposed to thrown) if their launcher
is the _primary_ wielded weapon. The only time a launcher in the
secondary slot is looked at is for autoquivering. So, yes, you can
two-weapon bow and katana, in that order; it means you're getting the
to-hit penalty in melee for bashing with the bow, though.

